<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  FalconPulsar Installer.app — Hardened Runtime entitlements.

  This file is passed to `codesign --options runtime --entitlements ...` when
  the installer is signed with a real Developer ID certificate (FP_SIGN=1).
  It activates Hardened Runtime with NO exceptions, which is the most
  restrictive (and thus most secure) configuration.

  The installer spawns /bin/bash, docker, and git via Process() — that is
  allowed under Hardened Runtime without any entitlement because the system
  tools it spawns are themselves signed by Apple or their vendor.

  If we ever embed a scripting interpreter (Python/Ruby/Node) or a JIT,
  we'll need to add exceptions here. For pure Swift + system-tool spawns,
  the empty dict is correct.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
